# macOS Finder metadata. One of these was committed at the root and
# nothing here would have stopped the next.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Editor and tooling backups.
**/*.bak

# tree-sitter build artifacts and the locally installed CLI. The
# lockfile is NOT one of them and is committed - it used to be listed
# below `*.dll` here, and that line was half of why the grammar job
# had nothing pinning anything. The other half was `--no-save` on the
# install line in ci.yml, which stops a lockfile being written at all;
# between them, no run of the job that gates every other job resolved
# the CLI or any transitive dependency against a recorded hash. Measured
# 2026-08-23: `npm install --prefix tree-sitter-axiom --no-save
# tree-sitter-cli` installed 0.26.13 - the `latest` dist-tag - while
# package.json asked for ^0.26.12, and wrote no lockfile. A lockfile is
# a source input, and `npm ci` cannot run without one.
tree-sitter-axiom/node_modules/
tree-sitter-axiom/*.dylib
tree-sitter-axiom/*.so
tree-sitter-axiom/*.dll

# The compiler a gate provisions for itself from `bootstrap/`, via
# `scripts/bootstrap-from-seed.sh --install`. Built, not committed -
# `bootstrap/` is the committed artifact.
.axiom-bin/
# The compiler `scripts/run-gates.sh` builds ONCE and every gate in a
# battery copies (`scripts/build-shared-axc.sh` writes the pair, `ci.yml`
# exports it as `AXIOM_AXC`). It sat untracked and unignored until
# 2026-09-04 - one `git add -A` after a battery away from a 2.4 MB
# binary in the history, which is how `.axiom-audit/` got there once.
.axiom-shared/

# Worktrees created by tooling.
.claude/worktrees/

# Python bytecode from the gate helpers under tests/.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Cargo's build artifacts. `rust/` is the only cargo project in this
# repository - it is the FFI's Rust side - so the pattern is scoped to
# it rather than written as a bare `target/` at the root: the compiler
# itself is written in Axiom and builds with `llc` and `cc`, and nothing
# outside rust/ produces a target/ directory. The generated `.ax`
# binding modules under rust/examples/*/axiom/ are NOT ignored: they are
# committed so `axiom check` and `axiom fmt` work on a checkout with no
# cargo, which is the same property scripts/bootstrap-from-seed.sh has.
rust/target/
rust/examples/*/target/

# The website under `web/`. `package-lock.json` is NOT here and is
# committed, for the reason the tree-sitter lockfile above is: the Pages
# workflow runs `npm ci`, which cannot run without one, and a build that
# resolves its own dependency versions is not reproducible.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.smoke-entry.tsx
web/.smoke-bundle.mjs
web/.tok-entry.ts
web/.tok-bundle.mjs

# `axiom run` builds into the WORKING DIRECTORY. self_host/main.ax:1668
# names the scratch executable `axiom_temp_output.<pid>`, and the
# `sysUnlink` that removes it is reached only after the child RETURNS.
# A clean run therefore leaves nothing and an interrupted one leaves
# the executable.
#
# REPRODUCED 2026-09-03, because the shape of the leak decides whether
# one line here is enough: `axiom run examples/web/server.ax 8961 1 1`
# from a scratch directory, then SIGTERM to the runner - a server is
# how you interrupt a `run`, since it is the program that does not
# return on its own - leaves `axiom_temp_output.99072`, mode 755, a
# 113,880-byte arm64 Mach-O. Only the executable: `buildToExecutable`
# removes its own `.ll`, `.o` and `.opt.ll`. That is exactly the shape
# of `examples/web/axiom_temp_output.92420`, a 156 KB arm64 Mach-O
# committed in d1e4a71, which lived in the tree until 2026-09-03 with
# every gate green because nothing was looking at the file list.
#
# This line stops the next one; `scripts/check-web.sh`'s hygiene sweep
# is what notices one committed past it, under any name.
axiom_temp_output.*
